<title>NETHERLANDS: COMMERCIAL UNION UNIT DELTA LLOYD H1 PROFIT.</title>
<headline>COMMERCIAL UNION UNIT DELTA LLOYD H1 PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per share (guilders)	    53.00   vs   49.88</p>
<p>    Net profit			     174.9    vs  164.6</p>
<p>    Turnover (bln)			   2.98   vs    2.69</p>
<p>Note - Full name is Delta Lloyd Verzekeringsgroep NV. The</p>
<p>insurer is a fully-owned subsidiary of U.K.'s Commercial Union</p>
<p>Assurance Plc .</p>
<p>Breakdown of turnover</p>
<p>    - Premium income life (bln)	   1.189    vs 1.008</p>
<p>    - Premium income non-life		 655    vs   634</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit				242.7  vs   220.5</p>
<p>    Tax						67.8  vs    55.9</p>
<p>Delta Lloyd reiterated an earlier forecast that it expected</p>
<p>a clearly higher net profit in 1997 compared to 1996.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
